&lt;h1&gt;


  One supplier change, 120 batches: building SpecCascade with FalkorDB
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;A project write-up for Graph Hacks: Context for AI Agents. Manufacturing records and enterprise actions described here are synthetic demonstrations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The question a recipe cannot answer
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A food manufacturer receives a supplier correction: two previously delivered cocoa lots contained a milk-derived component omitted from the original declaration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Searching current recipes for cocoa gives an incomplete picture. The operational decision depends on history: which lots were consumed, which recipe and artwork versions were used, and which customer shipments depend on the resulting stock?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SpecCascade investigates those connected facts, applies a targeted response and checks the execution independently.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Model the history behind the decision
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our FalkorDB graph links supplier notices to applicable ingredient lots, then connects those lots to historical production batches. Each batch links to its exact recipe and packaging version, allergen declaration, facility, warehouse, reservations and shipments. Shipments connect to orders and customers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Recipe membership and actual consumption are separate facts. Two batches can share a product family while consuming different delivered lots. Stopping both merely because they look similar would lose the precision the product is meant to provide.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Parameterized Cypher retrieves the connected manufacturing evidence. Stable source identifiers and versioned records preserve the provenance behind each finding.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  A controlled response with three classifications
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We created Northstar Foods with 120 synthetic batches, 12 products, three suppliers and two manufacturing facilities. The primary notice concerns two exact ingredient lots.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Graph traversal and policy evaluation identify 24 confirmed affected batches, four with unresolved consumption evidence and 92 unaffected by this notice. The unknown cases remain explicit. Twenty-eight batches require containment, while the other 92 retain eligibility.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These are measured results for a constructed dataset. We do not translate them into invented factory savings or claim real-world detection accuracy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Agents need bounded tools and shared evidence
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The application separates investigation, response coordination, recovery planning, independent verification and memory. Its OpenAI Agents SDK integration exposes bounded tools for policy inspection, memory retrieval, historical traversal, batch evidence, task creation, containment and verification.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Findings and tasks are shared through FalkorDB. Models receive actual tool results. Human QA authority and evidence requirements govern inventory disposition.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A reproducible local workflow executes the operational steps without a model credential, with the active mode visible in the product. The acceptance report records which provider behavior was actually verified; integration code alone is not treated as a successful model request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  A plan does not prove an ERP changed
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;FalkorDB records source evidence, decisions and intended actions. A separate transactional SQLite store records actual simulated inventory, holds, dispatches and dispositions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The coordinator applies holds, and dispatch of held stock is rejected. QA reviews supporting evidence and records a specific disposition. The verifier then re-queries source relationships and compares them with actual inventory, shipment and approval state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tests deliberately remove a required hold and fail an ERP write. A correct investigation cannot automatically pass execution verification.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Useful memory has an applicability boundary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A verified incident becomes a persistent episode connected to its investigation and evidence. A reusable procedure is recorded alongside it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Follow-up retrieval checks supplier, allergen, causal mechanism and memory validity. Prior experience can guide what to inspect; it cannot authorize clearance of new lots. The new investigation still traverses current relationships, and outdated episodes are excluded.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That boundary is visible in the demo: retrieved experience explains what can be reused and which previous conclusions must be rejected.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Proving the graph does real work
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Restricted-context mode cannot establish exposure or apply containment. During an actual FalkorDB outage, dependent endpoints return 503 instead of manufactured answers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Other tests change consumed lots, historical declarations, source completeness and shipment state. Outcomes change with those relationships. An ordinary restart check compares persisted graph, memory and enterprise state before and after restart.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Evaluation &amp;amp; Proof screen exposes executed Cypher, parameters, row counts and measured durations. A judge can inspect the evidence behind a result rather than rely on a confident explanation after the fact.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What we learned
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hardest engineering question was which evidence could justify an action. Historical causality, uncertainty and source versions mattered more than adding another metric.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We also learned to distinguish containment from resolution: an incident can be contained while lot documentation remains unresolved. Independent verification reports that boundary.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Finally, bounded tools and explicit authority make agent behavior easier to test, explain and trust within the scope of a synthetic demonstration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Next steps
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Future work includes ERPNext and supplier-mail adapters, reviewed document extraction, production identity and approval signatures, and stronger recovery of multi-system writes. Those are future integrations, not capabilities claimed by the current app.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SpecCascade targets &lt;strong&gt;Agents That Act on Connected Data&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Agent Memory and Coordination&lt;/strong&gt;. It was developed with Codex AI coding assistance; participant review, verification and technical understanding remain essential.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/Manikant92/SpecCascade" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Source, local setup, graph schema and verification evidence&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The first architecture diagram showed the parts of TDK CLI. This one shows time: what happens, in order, after you type &lt;code&gt;tdk up&lt;/code&gt;. Knowing the order tells you where a start can stop, and which message to read when it does.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The sequence below follows the repo's documented behaviour: the host check, the drift check before Tilt starts, the Starlark generation at Tilt load time, readiness, and the JSON result. Some steps are summarised, so check them against the code and the docs before you rely on one exact message.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The sequence
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;pre data-lang="mermaid"&gt;&lt;code&gt;sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Dev as Developer
    participant Agent as AI agent over MCP
    participant CLI as tdk CLI (TypeScript)
    participant Host as Host and container runtime
    participant Snap as Snapshots in .tdk-contract
    participant Tilt as Tilt
    participant Disc as Discovery (Starlark)
    participant Eng as Engine generators (Starlark)
    participant Dock as Docker
    participant Svc as Service containers

    Dev-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;CLI: tdk up (or agent calls up)
    Agent-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;CLI: up (MCP tool runs tdk up --json)

    CLI-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Host: check host type and container runtime
    alt canUp is false
        Host--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;CLI: no Docker, WebContainer, or Windows opt-in missing
        CLI--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Dev: exit non-zero, tell the reason, do not spawn Tilt
    else canUp is true
        CLI-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Snap: compare generated files with saved snapshots
        alt a generated file was hand-edited
            Snap--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;CLI: drift found, name the file
            CLI--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Dev: block the start, fix the source and retry
        else no drift
            CLI-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Tilt: spawn Tilt with the project Tiltfile
            Tilt-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Disc: load service.json files
            Disc--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Tilt: resources, stacks, dependsOn
            Tilt-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Eng: generate per-service runtime files
            Eng--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Tilt: write .autogenerated and service.yaml
            Tilt-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Dock: build images, start containers in order
            Dock-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Svc: start proxy, Postgres, services
            Svc--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Tilt: health route answers
            Tilt--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;CLI: resources report ready or failed
            CLI--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Agent: ok true, or ok false with errors
            CLI--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Dev: TDK is up, with URLs and ports
        end
    end

    Note over Agent,CLI: The agent polls status until readiness.ready is true
    Agent-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;CLI: status
    CLI--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Agent: readiness ready, pending, or failures
    Dev-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;CLI: tdk down
    CLI-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Tilt: stop resources
    Tilt-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;Dock: stop and remove containers&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  The steps that can stop you
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Four steps can stop a start, and each one tells you something different.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The host check.&lt;/strong&gt; If &lt;code&gt;canUp&lt;/code&gt; is false, the machine is the problem. No change to your project will help until the host has a working container runtime. The command exits without starting Tilt.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The drift check.&lt;/strong&gt; A hand edit to a file under &lt;code&gt;.autogenerated/&lt;/code&gt; blocks the start and names the file. The fix is upstream: change &lt;code&gt;service.json&lt;/code&gt; or the generator, then start again. This check runs before Tilt is spawned, so nothing has been built yet.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Readiness.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;up&lt;/code&gt; returns before the stack is ready, because a build can take longer than one command. The result tells you whether every resource is built, running, and healthy, or which one failed. &lt;code&gt;tdk status --json&lt;/code&gt; answers the same question at any time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The first failed resource.&lt;/strong&gt; A failure in one service usually stops the ones that depend on it. Read the logs for the first failed resource, not the last. &lt;code&gt;tdk logs --json --service &amp;lt;name&amp;gt; --tail 200&lt;/code&gt; returns a bounded snapshot.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Where the agent fits
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An agent does not replace this sequence. It calls the same commands through the MCP server. The useful part for the agent is the loop: call &lt;code&gt;up&lt;/code&gt;, poll &lt;code&gt;status&lt;/code&gt; until ready, read &lt;code&gt;logs&lt;/code&gt; for any failure, then stop. The sequence above shows why the poll is needed. &lt;code&gt;up&lt;/code&gt; returns before readiness.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Stopping cleanly
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;tdk down&lt;/code&gt; reverses the lifecycle: Tilt stops the resources, and Docker removes the containers. Run it when you finish. A stack left running keeps its ports, and the next &lt;code&gt;up&lt;/code&gt; may refuse to start while an old Tilt still answers on its port.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Summary
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One &lt;code&gt;tdk up&lt;/code&gt; is a short chain of checks before any container starts: host, drift, then generation and readiness. Each check has its own message, and each message points at the fix. Read them in order, and most starts become a matter of reading the first line that failed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


  Adding Groq‑Powered AI Summaries to the ISO‑27001 Dashboard with Daily Usage Limits
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; Integrated server‑side Groq calls to generate daily AI summaries for each analysis page, added a usage‑counter middleware and UI components (&lt;code&gt;AiButton&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;AiText&lt;/code&gt;). This keeps API keys secret, enforces a per‑day quota, and surfaces results without a full page reload.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The ISO‑27001 dashboard lets auditors view controls, policies, and daily logs. A recurring request from the team was to get an AI‑generated summary of each &lt;em&gt;analysis&lt;/em&gt; (&lt;code&gt;/analisis/[id]&lt;/code&gt;) that highlighted gaps and suggested next steps.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two technical blockers surfaced:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Secure AI calls:&lt;/strong&gt; The Groq API key was stored in the client bundle in an early prototype, causing CORS errors and exposing the secret.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Unlimited usage:&lt;/strong&gt; Groq charges per token, so we needed a hard daily limit per deployment to avoid runaway costs.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The symptom was a broken “Generate Summary” button that either threw a &lt;strong&gt;401 Unauthorized&lt;/strong&gt; (key exposed) or let anyone hammer the endpoint until the quota was exhausted, resulting in &lt;strong&gt;429 Too Many Requests&lt;/strong&gt; from Groq.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My first attempt was a &lt;strong&gt;client‑side fetch&lt;/strong&gt; from &lt;code&gt;components/ai-button.tsx&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// early prototype (removed)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;resp&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;Authorization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;`Bearer &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_GROQ_KEY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Issues:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;NEXT_PUBLIC_GROQ_KEY&lt;/code&gt; leaked into the bundle, visible in Chrome dev tools.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The request hit CORS restrictions because Groq does not allow the origin &lt;code&gt;localhost:3000&lt;/code&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;No server‑side throttling; every click hit the API directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I also tried wrapping the fetch in a &lt;strong&gt;Next.js API route&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;pages/api/ai.ts&lt;/code&gt;) but hit the same quota‑blow problem because the route lacked any persistence of usage counts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Result: the button either failed with a 401 or kept consuming tokens until the daily budget was spent, after which every call returned a 429.  &lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Store Secrets Server‑Side
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Added the Groq key to &lt;code&gt;.env.example&lt;/code&gt; (never committed the real value):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+ GROQ_API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
+ AI_DAILY_LIMIT=2000   # token budget per day
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The production &lt;code&gt;.env&lt;/code&gt; now contains the real key, and the code only accesses it via &lt;code&gt;process.env.GROQ_API_KEY&lt;/code&gt; on the server.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. Central AI Helper (&lt;code&gt;lib/ai.ts&lt;/code&gt;)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Created a thin wrapper around the Groq client that also tracks daily usage:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// lib/ai.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Groq&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;groq-sdk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/lib/db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;groq&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Groq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;apiKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;GROQ_API_KEY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;aiEnabled&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;GROQ_API_KEY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dailyLimit&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;AI_DAILY_LIMIT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/** Returns true if we have quota left for today */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;canUseAi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;():&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Promise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;used&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;selectFrom&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;ai_usage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;select&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;used&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toISOString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;slice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;executeTakeFirst&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;used&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dailyLimit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/** Increment usage counter */&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;recordAiUsage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tokens&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;insertInto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;ai_usage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toISOString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;slice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;used&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;raw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`COALESCE(used,0) + &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tokens&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;onConflictDoUpdate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;target&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="na"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;used&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;raw&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`ai_usage.used + &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tokens&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;execute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;ai_usage&lt;/code&gt; table is defined in &lt;code&gt;sql/schema.sql&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+ CREATE TABLE ai_usage (
+   date DATE PRIMARY KEY,
+   used INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0
+ );
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  3. Server Action (&lt;code&gt;app/(app)/analisis/actions.ts&lt;/code&gt;)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Next.js 13 server actions let us call the AI from a form without an explicit API route:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/(app)/analisis/actions.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use server&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;redirect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;next/navigation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;RuleError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;withParam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;errorMessage&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/lib/action-util&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;aiEnabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;aiModel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;buildContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;canUseAi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;recordAiUsage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;groq&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;@/lib/ai&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;generateSummary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;aiEnabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;RuleError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;AI not configured&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;canUseAi&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;RuleError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Daily AI quota exhausted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;buildContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;resp&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;groq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;chat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;completions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;aiModel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;messages&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;system&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;context&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}],&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;tokens&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;resp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;usage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;total_tokens&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;recordAiUsage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tokens&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Store the result in the DB (pseudo code)&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;db&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;updateTable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;analisis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;set&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;ai_summary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;resp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;choices&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;].&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;where&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;execute&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;redirect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`/analisis/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Key points:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;"use server"&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; guarantees the function runs only on the server, keeping the API key safe.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;canUseAi()&lt;/code&gt; checks the daily limit before any request.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;recordAiUsage()&lt;/code&gt; updates the &lt;code&gt;ai_usage&lt;/code&gt; table atomically.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Errors are thrown as &lt;code&gt;RuleError&lt;/code&gt; and surfaced by the UI component.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

