Tracks: &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track 01 (Agents That Act on Connected Data) &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track 02 (Agent Memory and Coordination) &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track 03 (Company Brain)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Live Cockpit&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a href="https://maelin-graph-hacks-demo.onrender.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://maelin-graph-hacks-demo.onrender.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;GitHub Repository&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a href="https://github.com/vivekyarra/Graph" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/vivekyarra/Graph&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Full Cypher Catalog&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a href="https://github.com/vivekyarra/Graph/blob/main/docs/CYPHER.md" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/vivekyarra/Graph/blob/main/docs/CYPHER.md&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Walkthrough Video&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a href="https://youtu.be/QCSNoWuLCNc" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://youtu.be/QCSNoWuLCNc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Executive Summary &amp;amp; The Core Thesis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a critical security alert fires—such as an active exploit path targeting a privileged IAM role—automated response systems usually do the most intuitive thing: quarantine the compromised service immediately.   In modern interconnected microservice architectures, this naive reflex is catastrophic. Taking down auth-service severs database pools, halts checkout transactions, breaks billing reconciliation, and locks out legitimate customers[cite: 1, 2]. An automated agent attempting to prevent a data breach ends up causing a self-inflicted $160,000/hour enterprise outage[cite: 2].   Next week, when a similar alert triggers, another automated workflow or engineer makes the exact same mistake[cite: 2]. Why? Because standard tools have no topology awareness, no persistent memory of past incidents, and no way to test containment plans safely[cite: 2].We built MAELIN to solve this fundamental dilemma[cite: 2].Our design philosophy is straightforward: Simulate before you remediate.[cite: 1, 2]MAELIN is an autonomous incident response engine whose sole shared brain is FalkorDB[cite: 2]. It proves containment mathematically using native graph algorithms, tests interventions on disposable graph clones without touching live production, remembers past postmortems across sessions using vector search, and grounds every single recommendation in verified graph evidence[cite: 2].&lt;br&gt;
[Security Alert] ──► [Bounded Multi-Hop Traversal] ──► [Choke-Point Cut Math] ──► [Counterfactual Clone Replay] ──► [Verified Surgical Fix][cite: 2]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F2i6lc7tridmdya9rlf33.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F2i6lc7tridmdya9rlf33.jpg" alt=" " width="799" height="500"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. System Architecture: Multi-Graph Isolation, Three Agents, Zero In-Memory State&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most multi-agent frameworks pass state in Python dictionaries, hidden memory buffers, or unstructured chat logs[cite: 2]. If an agent crashes or hallucinates, the reasoning chain is broken and unverifiable[cite: 2].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In MAELIN, agents maintain zero shared in-memory state[cite: 2]. Their only shared communication channel is FalkorDB[cite: 2].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multigraph Tenant Isolation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Using FalkorDB's multigraph architecture, each tenant operates across isolated graphs inside a single database instance:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;maelin__topology&lt;/strong&gt;: Stores live service dependencies, attack pivot edges, and organizational ownership records.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;maelin__memory&lt;/strong&gt;: Stores episodic incidents, semantic attack patterns, procedural playbooks, and multi-agent handoff ledgers[cite: 5, 6].&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;maelin_&lt;em&gt;sim&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Disposable sandbox clones created on demand via topo.copy() for counterfactual simulation[cite: 4, 5].&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Specialist Agent Pipeline&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;1.Recon &amp;amp; Graph Mapper Agent&lt;/strong&gt;: Executes protocol-level read-only queries (GRAPH.RO_QUERY) to discover all multi-hop exploit paths from external ingress points to privileged IAMRole and database targets[cite: 2]. It calculates betweenness centrality and evaluates the choke-point cut[cite: 2].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2.Episodic Memory Coordinator&lt;/strong&gt;: Queries the tenant's memory graph using cosine vector search over incident embeddings (db.idx.vector.queryNodes) and retrieves proven operational playbooks[cite: 2].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3.Explainable Remediation Agent&lt;/strong&gt;: Synthesizes the threat paths, customer blast radius, and memory evidence[cite: 2]. It runs candidate plans against an ephemeral database clone, validates minimal-cut optimality via Menger's theorem (algo.maxFlow), and outputs a verified surgical plan[cite: 2, 3].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each agent records its completed phase into an immutable (:Session)-[:HAS_HANDOFF]-&amp;gt;(:Handoff) graph transaction[cite: 3]:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight cypher"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;MATCH&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;s:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Session&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;id:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;$session_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;CREATE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;h:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Handoff&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;id:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;$handoff_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;from_agent:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;$from_agent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;to_agent:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;$to_agent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;phase:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;$phase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;evidence_ids:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;$evidence_ids&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="py"&gt;created_at:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;timestamp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="ss"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;CREATE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;:HAS_HANDOFF&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;RETURN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;h.id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;handoff_id&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If FalkorDB is unavailable, the entire API fails closed (HTTP 503); there are zero in-memory or SQLite fallbacks[cite: 3].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Few0ssbh06sfnyfpfxrow.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Few0ssbh06sfnyfpfxrow.png" alt=" " width="800" height="313"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Deep-Dive&lt;/strong&gt;: How FalkorDB &amp;amp; MCP Power the Agentic Core&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3.1 Model Context Protocol (FastMCP) Tool Layer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of allowing LLMs to execute raw, unvalidated queries, MAELIN exposes its FalkorDB reasoning engine through strictly typed FastMCP tools:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;inspect_attack_paths&lt;/strong&gt;: Executes read-only (GRAPH.RO_QUERY) bounded multi-hop reconnaissance and centrality scoring[cite: 2, 3].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;simulate_containment&lt;/strong&gt;: Spawns an isolated topo.copy() clone, applies candidate edge cuts, and verifies zero customer flow disruption[cite: 4, 5].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;recall_episodic_memory&lt;/strong&gt;: Performs vector similarity search (db.idx.vector.queryNodes) over past postmortems and computes causal policy shifts[cite: 2, 6].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;query_company_brain&lt;/strong&gt;: Runs hybrid full-text search (db.idx.fulltext.queryNodes) and ownership traversal across teams, engineers, ADRs, and postmortems[cite: 7].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;verify_agent_remediation&lt;/strong&gt;: Enforces the anti-hallucination barrier by checking that every cited asset matches a deterministic FalkorDB Evidence ID ([E1], [E2])[cite: 6, 7].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3.2 Bounded Variable-Length Traversal with Exact Provenance (Track 01)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Standard graph queries often return arbitrary node lists or fail to bound path search depths[cite: 3]. MAELIN executes strictly bounded variable-length Cypher traversals (CAN_PIVOT*1..7 and DEPENDS_ON*1..7), returning explicit nodes(p) and relationships(p) in a single round-trip[cite: 3]:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight cypher"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;MATCH&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;ing:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Asset&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;kind:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'ingress'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;:CAN_PIVOT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;..&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;target:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Asset&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;kind:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'identity'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;WHERE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;target.role&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'privileged'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;RETURN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;IN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;nodes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;id:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;n.id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="py"&gt;role:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;n.role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="py"&gt;kind:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;n.kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;}]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;path_nodes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
       &lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;IN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;relationships&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;path_edges&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;ORDER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;BY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;ASC&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;LIMIT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;[cite: 3]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By returning complete path provenance, every node and edge displayed in the cockpit or cited in an agent report is an exact, verifiable fact directly from the GraphBLAS engine[cite: 3].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3.3 Native Choke-Point Cut Math (Track 01)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
To determine which asset represents the single greatest point of exploit leverage, MAELIN pairs native betweenness centrality with path-cut mathematical aggregation[cite: 3]:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight cypher"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;CALL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;algo.betweenness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;([&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Asset'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'CAN_PIVOT'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;])&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;YIELD&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;score&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;RETURN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;node.id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;score&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;ORDER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;BY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;score&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;DESC&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;LIMIT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;[cite: 3]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Concurrently, MAELIN calculates the exact blast-radius reduction achieved by severing connections through a given vulnerable service[cite: 4]:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight cypher"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;MATCH&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;ing:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Asset&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;kind:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'ingress'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;:CAN_PIVOT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;..&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;svc:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Asset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;:CAN_PIVOT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;..&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;iam:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Asset&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;kind:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'identity'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;WHERE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;svc.id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;$chokepoint_service&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;WITH&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;DISTINCT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;paths_through_service&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;MATCH&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;ing:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Asset&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;kind:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'ingress'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;:CAN_PIVOT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;..&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;iam:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Asset&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;kind:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'identity'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;WITH&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;paths_through_service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;DISTINCT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;total_paths&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;RETURN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;paths_through_service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
       &lt;span class="n"&gt;total_paths&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
       &lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toFloat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;paths_through_service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;toFloat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;total_paths&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;100.0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;pct_blast_radius_eliminated&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;[cite: 4]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Remediation Agent directly incorporates this calculation into its findings[cite: 4]:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;"Isolating auth-service severs 1 of 1 (100.0%) active exploit paths to admin-role while preserving 100% of customer checkout and billing dependencies."[cite: 4]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3.4 Menger's Theorem Min-Cut via algo.maxFlow&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
How can an operator be certain that the agent's recommended cut is minimal and optimal?[cite: 4] MAELIN computes the edge connectivity between the threat ingress and the target identity using FalkorDB's native maximum flow algorithm[cite: 4]:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight cypher"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;CALL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;algo.maxFlow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Asset'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'CAN_PIVOT'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;$source_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;$target_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;YIELD&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;maxFlow&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;RETURN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;maxFlow&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;[cite: 4]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By Menger's Theorem, the maximum number of edge-disjoint paths between source and target equals the minimum number of edges whose removal disconnects them[cite: 4]. MAELIN checks the candidate plan's cut size against this theoretical lower bound[cite: 4]. If a plan requires 2 cuts and algo.maxFlow returns 2, MAELIN issues a cryptographic certificate that the intervention is mathematically optimal[cite: 4].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3.5 Counterfactual Simulation on Ephemeral Clones (Graph.copy())&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
The central breakthrough in MAELIN is the ability to simulate before executing[cite: 4].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of guessing whether an action will work or applying changes to live operational data, MAELIN dynamically clones the live topology graph in FalkorDB[cite: 5]:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 1. Spawn a dedicated, isolated sandbox graph
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sim_name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;maelin_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;tenant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;_sim_&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;uuid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;uuid4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;hex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;clone&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;topo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;copy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;sim_name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 2. Execute surgical Cypher deletions exclusively on the clone
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;candidate_plan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;actions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;clone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;cypher_mutation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 3. Re-traverse threat paths on the modified clone
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="n"&gt;remaining_routes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;clone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;
        MATCH p = (ing:Asset {kind: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;ingress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;})-[:CAN_PIVOT*1..7]-&amp;gt;(target:Asset {role: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;privileged&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;})
        RETURN count(p) AS remaining
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;result_set&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 4. Verify customer dependency preservation on the clone
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="n"&gt;disrupted_flows&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;clone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;
        MATCH (f:Asset {kind: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;business_flow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;})-[:DEPENDS_ON*1..7]-&amp;gt;(s:Asset)
        WHERE s.id IN $cut_services
        RETURN count(DISTINCT f) AS disrupted
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;cut_services&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;candidate_plan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;cut_service_ids&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;result_set&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 5. Assert containment: 2 routes reduced to 0, customer disruption = $0/hr
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="k"&gt;assert&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;remaining_routes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;][&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;assert&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;disrupted_flows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;][&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;finally&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 6. Guaranteed deterministic cleanup: sandbox deleted, live graph unmutated
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="n"&gt;clone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;delete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;[cite: 5]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This guarantees zero risk to live operations while providing empirical proof that containment will succeed[cite: 5].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3.6 Multi-Layered Memory with Cosine Vector Search (Track 02)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
MAELIN maintains a separate persistent memory catalog (maelin__memory) with three distinct layers[cite: 5]:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Episodic Memory (:Episode)&lt;/strong&gt;: Records past incidents, timestamped actions, and observed mean-time-to-remediate (MTTR)[cite: 6].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Semantic Memory (:SemanticPattern)&lt;/strong&gt;: Clusters structural attack topologies and maps recurring vulnerability patterns[cite: 6].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Procedural Memory (:Playbook)&lt;/strong&gt;: Indexes approved runbooks and verified intervention commands[cite: 6].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a new incident occurs, MAELIN embeds the incident context and performs a cosine vector similarity search directly inside FalkorDB[cite: 6]:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight cypher"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;CALL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;db.idx.vector.queryNodes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Episode'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'embedding'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;$query_vector&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;YIELD&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;score&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;MATCH&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;:RESOLVED_BY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;pb:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Playbook&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;RETURN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;node.incident_id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;incident_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
       &lt;span class="n"&gt;node.summary&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;summary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
       &lt;span class="n"&gt;pb.command&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;verified_command&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
       &lt;span class="n"&gt;score&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;ORDER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;BY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;score&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;DESC&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;[cite: 6]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Transparent Causal Policy Ablation&lt;br&gt;
When an operator logs that an intervention caused unforeseen downtime, MAELIN records the episode[cite: 6]. During subsequent investigations, the Pareto optimization engine recalculates expected utility[cite: 6].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The cockpit UI renders an explicit Causal Policy Ablation Banner, contrasting what the agent would have done without memory versus what it recommends with memory[cite: 6]:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;[WITHOUT MEMORY]&lt;/strong&gt;: Revoke admin-role (Estimated: $0/hr | &lt;strong&gt;Actual&lt;/strong&gt;: $160k/hr outage)[cite: 6]&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;[POLICY SHIFT] ──► [WITH MEMORY]&lt;/strong&gt;: Rotate auth credentials (Zero customer flow impact)[cite: 6]&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fandzbo65hjf9vrskd4z0.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fandzbo65hjf9vrskd4z0.jpg" alt=" " width="799" height="500"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3.7 Protocol-Level Safety &amp;amp; Anti-Hallucination Evidence IDs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;GRAPH.RO_QUERY Enforcement&lt;/strong&gt;: Every reconnaissance query executed by the Recon Agent calls g.ro_query(...) (GRAPH.RO_QUERY)[cite: 6]. FalkorDB automatically rejects any query containing mutating keywords (CREATE, SET, DELETE, MERGE) at the protocol level[cite: 6].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Deterministic Evidence IDs ([E1], [E2])&lt;/strong&gt;: Before the Remediation Agent synthesizes a response, MAELIN assigns deterministic evidence identifiers to all nodes returned by FalkorDB[cite: 6]. The output passes through an anti-hallucination verification barrier (verify_agent_remediation()) that verifies that every cited asset ID exists in the retrieved graph facts[cite: 6, 7]. If an LLM invents a fictitious service, the proposal is rejected before execution[cite: 7].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3.8 Company Brain: Organizational Knowledge Graph (Track 03)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;MAELIN extends the technical topology into an enterprise knowledge graph connecting[cite: 7]:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering Teams (:Team) and On-Call Staff (:Person)[cite: 7]&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architectural Decision Records (:Document {kind: 'adr'})[cite: 7]&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incident Postmortems (:Document {kind: 'postmortem'})[cite: 7]&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Users can ask plain-language questions like "Who owns customer-db and what runbooks apply?" in the BRAIN tab[cite: 7]. MAELIN executes a hybrid full-text Cypher query (db.idx.fulltext.queryNodes) combined with ownership traversal and returns cited answers linked directly to the on-call engineer and approved runbook[cite: 7]:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users can ask plain-language questions like "Who owns customer-db and what runbooks apply?" in the BRAIN tab[cite: 7]. MAELIN executes a hybrid full-text Cypher query (db.idx.fulltext.queryNodes) combined with ownership traversal and returns cited answers linked directly to the on-call engineer and approved runbook[cite: 7]:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight cypher"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;CALL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;db.idx.fulltext.queryNodes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Document'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;$search_query&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;YIELD&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;doc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;score&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;MATCH&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;doc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;:GOVERNS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;asset:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Asset&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ss"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;id:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;$asset_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;:OWNS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;team:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;:MEMBER_OF&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;person:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Person&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;OPTIONAL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;MATCH&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;asset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;:HAS_RUNBOOK&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="py"&gt;pb:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Playbook&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;RETURN&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;asset.id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;service&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
       &lt;span class="n"&gt;team.name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;owning_team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
       &lt;span class="n"&gt;person.name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;on_call_responder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
       &lt;span class="n"&gt;doc.title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;governance_doc&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
       &lt;span class="n"&gt;doc.kind&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;doc_kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
       &lt;span class="n"&gt;pb.command&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;AS&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;runbook_command&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="ss"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
       &lt;span class="n"&gt;score&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;ORDER&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;BY&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;score&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;DESC&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;LIMIT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F5yi51u4y9edg3qh2wxkn.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F5yi51u4y9edg3qh2wxkn.jpg" alt=" " width="799" height="500"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. The Lumen Edge Cockpit &amp;amp; Developer Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
We designed MAELIN's interface around the Lumen Edge design language—a single-screen incident cockpit featuring sub-chromatic engineered glass, deep graphite surfaces (#0b0c10), soft radial gradients, and an interactive 3D graph visualization canvas[cite: 7, 8].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Top HUD Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;: algo.maxFlow = 2 · Betweenness = 0.85 · pageRank = 0.427 · FalkorDB connected
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;3D Graph Canvas&lt;/strong&gt;: Interactive Force/Orbit topology mapping (ingress) -&amp;gt; [auth-service] -&amp;gt; (admin-role) and [customer-db]   &lt;strong&gt;Recommended Containment&lt;/strong&gt;: [B] Cut auth -&amp;gt; billing · Cost: $0/hr (was $160k/hr)
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Choke-Point Cut Math&lt;/strong&gt;: auth-service severs 100% of exploit paths
&lt;strong&gt;FalkorDB Telemetry&lt;/strong&gt;: GRAPH.RO_QUERY: 0.84 ms · algo.maxFlow: 1.12 ms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key UI Features&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Interactive 3D Perspective&lt;/strong&gt;: Pan, tilt, zoom, and orbit the graph topology[cite: 8]. Compromised routes pulse with animated laser traces[cite: 8].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Execution Telemetry Drawer&lt;/strong&gt;: Displays server-side run_time_ms reported directly by FalkorDB's GraphBLAS engine for every query[cite: 8].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;1-Click Reset &amp;amp; Scenario Ingestion&lt;/strong&gt;: Easily reset synthetic state or import custom topology JSON files without leaving the browser[cite: 8].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Accessible High-Contrast Controls&lt;/strong&gt;: High-contrast selection dropdowns (#0b0c10), HUD intel chips left-aligned, and legend pinned right with zero layout shift (CLS = 0)[cite: 8].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Verification &amp;amp; Testing Rigor&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We subjected MAELIN to rigorous automated testing across 16 test modules[cite: 8]:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Offline test suite (109 passed, 13 skipped live integration, 0 failures)&lt;/span&gt;
python &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-m&lt;/span&gt; pytest &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-q&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Full test suite with live FalkorDB integration&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nv"&gt;FALKOR_INTEGRATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;1 python &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-m&lt;/span&gt; pytest &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-q&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;[cite: 8]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test Suite Highlights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;-** Property-Based Randomized DAG Oracle (test_stress.py)**: Runs 5,000 synthetic random DAG topologies, comparing Cypher traversal results against an independent mathematical oracle[cite: 8].&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Clone Isolation &amp;amp; Leak Prevention (test_simulation.py)&lt;/strong&gt;: Verifies that disposable clones use dynamic UUIDs, delete reliably during exceptions, and leave the primary graph unmutated[cite: 8].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Security &amp;amp; Fail-Closed Guardrails (test_hardening.py, test_challenger_security.py)&lt;/strong&gt;: Verifies constant-time token authentication (hmac.compare_digest), tenant regex bounds, and strict HTTP 503 shutdown when FalkorDB is offline[cite: 8].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. What We Learned Building on FalkorDB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;GraphBLAS is Unmatched for Agent Loops&lt;/strong&gt;: Multi-agent workflows require low latency[cite: 8]. While standard graph databases take tens of milliseconds per hop, FalkorDB's C-based GraphBLAS matrix multiplication engine consistently returned complex 5-hop traversals in under 1 millisecond[cite: 8, 9].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Graph.copy() Enables Risk-Free Agent Autonomy&lt;/strong&gt;: The biggest barrier to deploying autonomous AI agents in production is the fear of unintended mutations[cite: 9]. Having native, sub-second graph cloning built into the database allows agents to simulate and prove safety before executing[cite: 9].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Graphs Prevent Agent Hallucinations&lt;/strong&gt;: When LLMs query vector databases alone, they lack topological constraints[cite: 9]. By grounding the agent in explicit Cypher relationships, every conclusion is provable, traceable, and explainable[cite: 9].&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

